{{! Twennie Terms and Conditions }}
{{#*inline "title"}}Terms and Conditions | Twennie{{/inline}}

<section class="terms-conditions-section">
  <div class="terms-conditions-container">
    <h1 class="terms-conditions-title">Twennie Terms and Conditions</h1>

    <!-- =====================================================
         COMMUNITY CONDUCT
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Leader and Group Member Conduct</h2>

    <p>
      Twennie is a collaborative professional learning platform. All leaders and group members are expected to engage in good faith, with professionalism, generosity, and respect.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Respectful Participation:</strong> Treat all members with courtesy and professionalism. Disagreement is acceptable; disrespect is not.</li>
      <li><strong>No Harassment or Abuse:</strong> Harassment, bullying, discrimination, intimidation, or exclusionary behavior is not tolerated.</li>
      <li><strong>Constructive Collaboration:</strong> Learning activities should be approached with openness, generosity, and a willingness to support others.</li>
      <li><strong>Responsible Feedback:</strong> Feedback must be relevant, constructive, and aligned with professional growth.</li>
      <li><strong>Accountability:</strong> Conflicts should be addressed respectfully. Violations may be reported to Twennie administrators.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- =====================================================
         CONTENT OWNERSHIP & LICENSING
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Content Ownership and Intellectual Property</h2>

    <p>
      Any content you create or upload to Twennie — including articles, videos, interviews, prompt sets, exercises, templates, missions, nuggets, or related learning units — remains <strong>your intellectual property</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Submitting content to Twennie grants Twennie a limited license to host, display, and distribute that content <em>solely for learning and development purposes</em>, in accordance with the visibility settings you select.
    </p>

    <p>
      Content submitted with all-member visibility may be accessed by other Twennie members for learning purposes only. Twennie will not use member-created content for promotional or marketing purposes without explicit consent.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         CONTENT APPROVAL & REMOVAL
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Content Review and Approval</h2>

    <p>
      All submitted content is subject to review by Twennie administrators. Approval decisions may consider relevance, educational value, clarity, format, length, and subject matter.
    </p>

    <p>
      Twennie reserves the right to reject, remove, or request revisions to any content at its discretion. Members may contact Twennie for guidance prior to resubmission.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         VISIBILITY & RISK
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Visibility Settings and Risk Awareness</h2>

    <p>
      Twennie provides three visibility options for content: <strong>group-only</strong>, <strong>organization-only</strong>, and <strong>all members</strong>. You select visibility for each unit you create.
    </p>

    <p>
      Twennie is a learning platform — <strong>not a document repository</strong>. Members should never upload proprietary, confidential, competitive, or regulated information under any visibility mode.
    </p>

    <p>
      Twennie cannot guarantee protection against misuse or infringement once content is visible to others. Members concerned about intellectual property risk should avoid all-member visibility.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         LIABILITY & INFRINGEMENT
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Liability and Copyright Responsibility</h2>

    <p>
      Twennie is not responsible for plagiarism, misuse, or infringement of member-posted content. Legal enforcement of intellectual property rights remains the sole responsibility of the content creator.
    </p>

    <p>
      Members agree that Twennie, its administrators, owners, and employees are not liable for losses resulting from content sharing decisions made by members.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         CANCELLATION & CONTENT RETENTION
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Membership Cancellation and Content Retention</h2>

    <p>
      Upon cancellation, members may request removal of their submitted content. While deletion tools are not available within the platform, Twennie will honor reasonable deletion requests submitted directly.
    </p>

    <p>
      Twennie encourages continued inclusion of previously approved content in the learning library, but will not prevent members from publishing or using their content elsewhere.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         CITATION & EXTERNAL USE
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Citations and External Use</h2>

    <p>
      Any use of Twennie member content outside the Twennie platform requires direct permission from the author. Responsibility for proper citation and consent rests with the requesting party.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         REPORTING & ANALYTICS
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Learning Activity Reporting</h2>

    <p>
      Submitting content or participating in learning activities implies consent for anonymized inclusion in internal analytics and reports, such as completion rates or engagement trends.
    </p>

    <p>
      No organization or individual will be identified in promotional materials without explicit written consent.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         INDIVIDUAL MEMBERS
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Individual Membership Visibility</h2>

    <p>
      Individual members do not belong to groups or organizations. Content shared by individual members is visible only to themselves unless explicitly shared with all members.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         PLATFORM SECURITY & TECHNICAL SAFEGUARDS
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Platform Security and Technical Safeguards</h2>

    <p>
      Twennie employs industry-standard technical and organizational measures to protect user accounts, learning data, and platform integrity. These safeguards include:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Authentication Controls:</strong> Secure login mechanisms, including optional multi-factor authentication (MFA) where available.</li>
      <li><strong>Session Protection:</strong> Measures to prevent session hijacking and unauthorized access.</li>
      <li><strong>CSRF Protection:</strong> Cross-site request forgery protections for authenticated actions.</li>
      <li><strong>Role-Based Access Controls:</strong> Separation of permissions for members, group leaders, administrators, and organization administrators.</li>
      <li><strong>Data Segmentation:</strong> Logical separation of group, organization, and all-member content.</li>
      <li><strong>Audit and Monitoring:</strong> Administrative oversight and logging to detect misuse or policy violations.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      While Twennie takes reasonable steps to secure the platform, no system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Members are responsible for safeguarding their credentials and choosing appropriate visibility settings.
    </p>

    <!-- =====================================================
         FINAL STATEMENT
    ====================================================== -->
    <h2>Your Trust Matters</h2>

    <p>
      Twennie exists to support learning, collaboration, and professional growth — not to extract, monetize, or harvest proprietary information. Protecting your trust, your work, and your professional integrity is foundational to the platform.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>


{{#if user}}

  {{#unless user.termsAccepted}}
    <form method="POST" action="/termsconditions/accept" style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 720px;">
      {{#if csrfToken}}
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrfToken}}">
      {{/if}}

      <input type="hidden" name="next" value="{{next}}">

      <label style="display:flex; gap:0.75rem; align-items:flex-start;">
        <input
          type="checkbox"
          name="acceptTerms"
          required
          style="margin-top: 0.25rem;"
        >
        <span>
          I have read and agree to Twennie’s Terms &amp; Conditions.
        </span>
      </label>

      <button type="submit" class="contribute-btn" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        accept and continue
      </button>
    </form>

  {{else}}
    <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 720px; text-align:center;">
      <p style="font-weight:600; margin: 0;">
        you have already accepted the terms &amp; conditions
      </p>
    </div>
  {{/unless}}

{{else}}

  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 720px; text-align:center;">
    <p style="font-weight:600;">
      please log in to accept the terms &amp; conditions
    </p>
    <a
      href="/login"
      class="contribute-btn"
      style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none;"
    >
      log in
    </a>
  </div>

{{/if}}





  </section>


